{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788171342,"nonce":"TIrN2YhXBP1awFyWLyq9ASVcQXE=","title":"ci: the dogfood `lint` gate has no fixed definition of \"formatted\" — `scarab-pipeline` is already 9 diffs red on current stable","message":"`.scarab/dogfood.yaml`'s `lint` step runs, as its first command:\n\n    cargo fmt -p scarab-identity -p scarab-pipeline -- --check\n\nThat command FAILS today on the tree at `main`:\n\n    scarab-identity   0 rustfmt diffs   (clean)\n    scarab-pipeline   9 rustfmt diffs   crates/scarab-pipeline/src/lib.rs\n                                        (lines ~974, 1932, 2575, 2700, 2713,\n                                         2723, 2730, 3266, 3301)\n\nIt passes on the demo box only because `rust:1-bookworm` ships an older rustfmt\nthan current stable (`rustfmt 1.9.0-stable`, 2026-07-07). Nobody's PR did this\nand nobody's PR will fix it — the next rust-image bump turns the step red for\neveryone at once.\n\n\n`rust-toolchain.toml` pins `channel = \"stable\"` — a MOVING channel — and there is\nno `rustfmt.toml` in the repo, so formatting is whatever the current rustfmt's\nbuilt-in defaults happen to be. A `--check` gate whose definition of \"correct\"\nchanges underneath it is not a gate; it is a timer.\n\nIt also gets worse rather than better on a future bump. Measured on the same\nfile:\n\n    --style-edition 2015    9 diffs\n    --style-edition 2021    9 diffs   (the effective default today)\n    --style-edition 2024   22 diffs\n\n\nThis workspace is deliberately NOT fmt-clean as a whole — a repo-wide\n`cargo fmt` churns ~90 unrelated files, which is exactly why the dogfood lint\nstep scopes itself to the two crates that WERE clean. One of them has since\ndrifted. The narrowing was the right call and it silently stopped being true.\n\n\n1. Add a `rustfmt.toml` pinning `style_edition` (and anything else the repo\n   relies on), and format `scarab-pipeline`. Fixes both halves: the gate stops\n   floating AND the crate goes clean. The churn is confined to one file's 9\n   sites, not 90 files.\n2. Format `scarab-pipeline` only. Clears the red, leaves the gate floating —\n   this recurs on the next toolchain bump.\n3. Drop `scarab-pipeline` from the lint step's scope. Honest but shrinking: the\n   gate then covers one crate.\n4. Pin `channel` to an exact version in `rust-toolchain.toml`. Fixes the float\n   repo-wide, but couples every contributor to a version bump cadence — a\n   bigger decision than this ticket.\n\n(1) looks right. Not doing it here because formatting a crate is a diff someone\nshould choose to own, and because `rustfmt.toml` affects every crate in the\nworkspace, not just this gate.\n\n\n    cargo fmt -p scarab-identity -p scarab-pipeline -- --check   # exit 1\n    rustfmt --version                                            # 1.9.0-stable\n\nFound while verifying PRs #4/#5 (the CI-does-too-much work): the `scarab` commit\nstatus was red on both, and ruling my own diff out meant running the dogfood\npipeline's commands locally. My change touched only `scarab-executor-local`, so\nthis is unrelated to it — and unrelated to whatever is actually failing on the\ndemo box, which returns 401 and was never read.","files":null}]}